Answer: The DisplayImpl class implements the Display interface and provides the body for display().Sample Input: No input.Sample Output:Hello from DisplayImpl.

```java
interface Display {
void display();
}
class DisplayImpl implements Display {
@Override
public void display() {
System.out.println("Hello from DisplayImpl.");
}
}
public class Main {
public static void main(String[] args) {
Display displayRef = new DisplayImpl();
displayRef.display();
}
}
```

Answer: The DisplayImpl class is declared inside Launch and implements Display. An instance of the inner class is assigned to a Display reference.Sample Input: No input.Sample Output:Hello from inner class.

```java
interface Display {
void display();
}
class Launch {
class DisplayImpl implements Display {
@Override
public void display() {
System.out.println("Hello from inner class.");
}
}
public static void main(String[] args) {
Launch launch = new Launch();
Display displayRef = launch.new DisplayImpl();
displayRef.display();
}
}
```

